ialectal differences. The course focuses on oral and written skills, with emphasis on tasks based on familiar contexts of use. It also introduces learners to the history, culture and geography of the Andes through exposure to cultural practices, proverbs, folklore, and artefacts of the region (e.g. textiles). Students will reflect on Quechua as an endangered language and on the significance of keeping this very popular indigenous language of Latin America alive.", "catalogBreadth": null, "catalogDistr": "(FL-AG)", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2881, "crseId": 369277, "crseOfferNbr": 3, "subject": "LATA", "catalogNbr": "1951", "titleShort": "Foreign Policy as Subversion", "titleLong": "Foreign Policy as Subversion", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 10195, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "01:25PM", "timeEnd": "02:40PM", "startDt": "08/26/2024", "endDt": "12/09/2024", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "rbc23", "firstName": "Raymond", "middleName": "B.", "lastName": "Craib"}, {"instrAssignSeq": 2, "netid": "tl14", "firstName": "Tamara", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Loos"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Baker Laboratory 219", "bldgDescr": "Baker Laboratory", "facilityDescrshort": "BKL219", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "08/26/2024", "endDt": "12/21/2024",